---
// The page's masthead: the internal-only utility strip, the way back to the
// status page, and the title block.
//
// The back link is `withBase`d rather than relative. The page it replaced was a
// raw public/ file that could not read Astro's BASE_URL and had to hand-write
// `./review/index.html`; as a real route that constraint is gone, and a
// base-aware link is what keeps it working under the review track's subpath.
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
---

<div class="util">Internal · the plan for moving the domain, and where we've got to</div>

<header class="page">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="back"><a href={withBase('/review/index.html')}>← Project status &amp; decisions</a></div>
    <div class="kick">Domain Cutover Runbook</div>
    <h1>Moving harvardintech.com to the new site</h1>
    <p>
      What it takes to point the real domain at the site we've built, in the
      order it has to happen, with the exact values for whoever sits in the
      GoDaddy console — and what we need from you before anyone can start.
    </p>
    <div class="meta">
      DNS discovery 2026-07-02 · steps S1–S9 · decisions D1–D5 · checks V1–V6 · rollback R1–R3
    </div>
  </div>
</header>
